# The sdist's manifest. `git archive`'s `export-ignore` lines in `.gitattributes` do not reach an
# sdist, which the `build` job builds from a checkout, so the classes those lines keep out of the
# source archive need their own statement here.
#
# The two lock renderings ship beside the package: the release procedure checks the sdist lists both
# (`post-build-check`, DR-7 clause (iii)), and an sdist that carries `pylock.toml` and
# `requirements.txt` installs the reviewed resolution rather than the one a user's moment resolves.
include pylock.toml requirements.txt

# The test tree is `private-estate`'s excluded class AC-2, and setuptools' sdist defaults put the
# top-level `tests/test*.py` files in the archive. Pruning the directory makes "excluded" true of the
# sdist as the release-state table states it, so no release ships a test file.
prune tests
